1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,400
Why Domain Matters, part 1: Retail and grocery. The record says 55 bags on hand; the shelf has been empty since Wednesday.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:10,800
Each post takes one real failure and follows it through the people who see it differently.

3
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:17,200
A fictional supermarket in Jayanagar, Bengaluru. Every number comes from a synthetic, seeded world.

4
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:24,600
The cases sat behind the rice. The books never fell to the reorder point, so nothing was ordered.

5
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:31,000
One name, four numbers: availability of 97%, 75%, 77% or 78%.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:37,400
The demo runs the same month on the same customers. Change what the store does and every view updates.

7
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:43,800
The store manager sees an empty bay, and a handheld that says 55.

8
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:50,200
The reorder system sees 55 bags above its reorder point. In stock, no reorder needed, three nights running.

9
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:56,600
The planner sees sales fall 59%, and the forecast slides to 20.2 bags a day.

10
00:00:56,600 --> 00:01:02,000
The supplier sees orders drop from 172 to 112 bags a week.

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,400
What actually happened: 14 cases behind the rice, 39 open hours with an empty shelf, 71 bags not sold.

12
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:15,800
A low-sales alert, checked next morning: lost bags fall from 157 to 90.

13
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:22,200
Scanned backroom bins prevent it: 157 lost bags become 1.

14
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:29,600
The records behind it. Nothing says “misplaced”. Download them and find the gap yourself.

15
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:37,500
Milk carries the opposite risk. A 5% leaner order lifts milk’s margin from ₹4,121 to ₹10,810, and 150 more pouches go unfound.

16
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:43,900
Each post ends with a learning path: real books, real datasets, and practice on the store’s records.

17
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:49,400
Every system keeps a record. Domain knowledge is knowing when the record is wrong.
